  "dataQuality": "partial",
  "notes": "Boss teams are the DEFAULT (Normal) difficulty first-time teams from the official 'Default Mode Bosses v4.1 (with EVs)' documentation, read via a public Scribd text export of that sheet (the original Google Drive/Docs files were not used). Gym teams for Brock and Misty are complete (4 Pokemon each, as documented). For Lt. Surge, Erika, Sabrina, Koga, Blaine and Clair the sheet's text rendering truncates the 5th team member's name to a single letter, so each of those teams lists only the 4 fully readable members; the omitted 5th member was not guessed. Lt. Surge's levelCap (33) is the highest level among his captured members; the in-game level cap for that fight is 34, held by the unresolved 5th member. Sabrina's fight is a doubles battle and Blaine's is fought in permanent sun, per the sheet. A few of Sabrina's move assignments were reconstructed from a garbled text rendering and may be imperfect. Elite Four members each have two documented team variants; the first-listed variant is used (Lorelei: her rain team). Lorelei's battles are doubles. The Champion's team depends on the rival's starter: the Koraidon variant (rival started with Squirtle) is used here; in the other variants Miraidon replaces Koraidon with the rest of the team unchanged. Rematch teams, Johto leaders, rival/Rocket/miniboss fights and postgame bosses from the same documentation are NOT included. Encounters come from PokePorto's locations page: day and night pools are merged into one pool per area, Mt. Moon's three floors are merged (identical level ranges), and cosmetic variants (Burmy cloaks, Deerling seasons, Pumpkaboo sizes, Minior cores) are collapsed to the base species. Encounter coverage runs from Route 1 through Route 7 (the approach to Celadon City / 4th gym) and stops there; Celadon City itself, Pokemon Tower, and all later areas are not included. The PokePorto page does not state which game version its tables reflect, so encounter data may lag v4.1 slightly.",
